## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model a device-resident telemetry system that serves multiple apps while enforcing data minimization and consent, balancing privacy, UX impact, and backend savings.

## Key Concepts

- Data deduplication and cross-app coordination on-device
- Consent lifecycle and policy enforcement across tenants
- On-device aggregation, sampling, and energy budgeting
- Privacy/compliance costs and drift monitoring
- Rollout strategy, break-even analysis, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
function aggregateDeltas(deltas) {
  // de-duplicate by user/app+event, then sample
  const seen = new Set();
  const out = [];
  for (const d of deltas) {
    const key = d.userId + '|' + d.appId + '|' + d.eventId;
    if (!seen.has(key)) {
      seen.add(key);
      if (Math.random() < d.sampleRate) out.push(d.aggregate);
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify cross-app dedup cost vs backend savings?
- What would a staged rollout look like to minimize risk and ensure compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to translate product goals into a concrete cost model that accounts for on-device constraints, security requirements, and regulatory concerns. It also probes understanding of trade-offs for multi-app isolation, update mechanics, and privacy-by-design principles.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML model footprints and TEE (Trusted Execution Environment) architecture
- Cross-app isolation with per-app policy overrides
- Telemetry budgeting and data minimization under privacy regulations
- OTA update economics, delta patching, and cryptographic key rotation
- Compliance frameworks (GDPR, CCPA), privacy-by-design, and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-break-even calculator
function needsGoNoGo(serverSavingsPerMonth, deviceCostsPerMonth, months) {
  const netSavings = serverSavingsPerMonth - deviceCostsPerMonth;
  const cumulativeSavings = netSavings * months;
  return {
    breakEvenMonths: deviceCostsPerMonth / netSavings,
    go: cumulativeSavings > 0 && months >= 18
  };
}
```

